    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0564" n="542" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg542"/>

                <head>No. 77.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Earl Granville to Sir E.
                        Thornton.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-31"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 31,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[From British Blue Book “North America,” No. 9, (1872,) p.
                    33.]</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I send you the draught of a Convention for
                    adjourning the period for the presentation of the arguments under the Vth
                    Article of the Treaty of Washington, to be used, however, by you only in case of
                    the new Treaty Article proposed by us not being agreed to, and an adjournment
                    being agreed to, in which case you are authorized to sign it as it is now sent
                    to you.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GRANVILLE.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d212-a1.xml" xpointer="d212-a1"/>
            </div>
